<Qucs Library 0.0.22 "MESFETs">

<Component MESFETCL1>
  <Description>
Simple level 1 Curtice MESFET model (ngspice).
1. Curtice level 1 I-V core as ngspice B sources: DC, transient and AC,
2. Fixed capacitors: cgs (through rin), cgd and cds,
3. Parasitic R and L components: rd, ld, rg, lg, rs and ls.

The drain current, from drain to source inside the parasitics:
  Ids = beta (Vgs - vto)^2 (1 + lambda Vds) tanh(alpha Vds) for Vgs > vto, else 0.
The gate current, from gate to source:
  Igs = -area is + Vgs / 1 GOhm below vbi; above it, rising by
  (Vgs - vbi) / rf from there.
These are the equations of the XSPICE code model curtice1 (Mike Brinson,
2016) that an earlier library of this name compiled at run time; written
as B sources, the part needs no compiler. Two changes: the gate current is
continuous at vbi (the code model jumped there to vbi/rf, 0.1 A, and a
transient could stop on the jump), and each lead inductance has 1 kOhm
across it, damping the leads' resonance with the capacitors (at GHz) that
a transient in microsecond steps rang on ("Timestep too small"); 0.1 nH is
6 Ohm at 10 GHz, so the 1 kOhm leaves the part's response as it was.

Parameters:

NAME	DESCRIPTION				DEFAULT VALUE
beta	Transconductance parameter		3m	A/V^2
lambda	Channel length modulation
	parameter for quadratic model		50m	1/V
alpha	Coefficient of Vds in tanh
	function for quadratic model		2.25	1/V
vto	Quadratic model gate threshold
	voltage					-1.8	V
area	Area factor (of the gate's
	reverse current)			1
rg	External gate resistance			5.1	Ohm
rd	External drain resistance			1.3	Ohm
rs	External source resistance			1.3	Ohm
is	Gate diode saturation current		1f	A
rf	Gate forward bias slope
	resistance				10	Ohm
vbi	Built-in gate potential			1	V
ld	External drain lead inductance		0.1n	H
lg	External gate lead inductance		0.1n	H
ls	External source lead inductance		0.1n	H
cgs	Gate-source capacitance			1p	F
cgd	Gate-drain capacitance			1p	F
cds	Drain-source capacitance			1p	F
rin	Series resistance to cgs			1m	Ohm

References:
1. W.R. Curtice, A MESFET model for use in the design of GaAs integrated circuits, IEEE
Transactions on Microwave Theory and Techniques, MTT-28, pp. 448-456, 1980.
2. Mike Brinson and Stefan John, Qucs: Compact device - circuit macromodel specification; A
Curtice level 1 MESFET model, pp 1-8, 2007.
3. Mike Brinson, Qucs: A report - Verilog-A compact device models for GaAs MESFETS, pp 1-38, 2008.
  </Description>
  <Model>
.Def:MESFETs_MESFETCL1 nd ns ng beta="3e-3" lambda="0.05" alpha="2.25" vto="-1.8" area="1" rg="5.1" rd="1.3" rs="1.3" is="1e-15" rf="10.0" vbi="1.0" ld="0.1e-9" lg="0.1e-9" ls="0.1e-9" cgs="1e-12" cgd="1e-12" cds="1e-12" rin="1e-3"
.Def:End
  </Model>
  <Spice>* Qucs 0.0.22  MESFETs_MESFETCL1.sch

.SUBCKT MESFETs_MESFETCL1  gnd nd ns ng beta=3e-3 lambda=0.05 alpha=2.25 vto=-1.8 area=1 rg=5.1 rd=1.3 rs=1.3 is=1e-15 rf=10.0 vbi=1.0 ld=0.1e-9 lg=0.1e-9 ls=0.1e-9 cgs=1e-12 cgd=1e-12 cds=1e-12 rin=1e-3
* The drain current, Curtice level 1 (quadratic): from nd1 to ns1.
B1 nd1 ns1 I = V(ng1,ns1) > {vto} ? {beta}*(V(ng1,ns1)-{vto})*(V(ng1,ns1)-{vto})*(1+{lambda}*V(nd1,ns1))*tanh({alpha}*V(nd1,ns1)) : 0
* The gate current: below vbi, the reverse current and 1 nS; above it, rising with the slope 1/rf.
B2 ng1 ns1 I = V(ng1,ns1) > {vbi} ? (V(ng1,ns1)-{vbi})/{rf}-{area}*{is}+1e-9*{vbi} : -{area}*{is}+1e-9*V(ng1,ns1)
R2 ng1  ng2 {rg}
R4 ns1  _net0 {rin}
C2 ng1  _net0 {cgs}
C1 nd1  ng1 {cgd}
R1 ns1 ns2  {rs}
L3 ns2  ns {ls}
R3 nd1  nd2 {rd}
C3 nd1  ns1 {cds}
L2 nd  nd2 {ld}
L1 ng  ng2 {lg}
* (The leads damped: their resonance with the capacitors rang in a transient.)
RL1 ng  ng2 1k
RL2 nd  nd2 1k
RL3 ns2  ns 1k
.ENDS
  </Spice>
<SpiceAttach >
  <Symbol>
    <Line -20 -20 0 40 #aa0000 3 1>
    <Line -40 0 20 0 #000080 2 1>
    <.PortSym -40 0 3 0>
    <Line -20 -10 20 0 #aa0000 3 1>
    <Line -20 10 20 0 #aa0000 3 1>
    <Line 0 -10 0 -30 #aa0000 3 1>
    <Line 0 40 0 -30 #aa0000 3 1>
    <.PortSym 0 40 2 0>
    <.PortSym 0 -40 1 0>
    <Text -12 -24 8 #aa0000 0 "d">
    <Text -10 11 8 #aa0000 0 "s">
    <Text -33 -15 8 #aa0000 0 "g">
    <Text 28 -33 8 #aa0000 270 "CURTICE L1">
    <.ID 50 -116 MESFETCL1 "1=beta=3e-3==" "1=lambda=0.05==" "1=alpha=2.25==" "1=vto=-1.8==" "1=area=1==" "1=rg=5.1==" "1=rd=1.3==" "1=rs=1.3==" "1=is=1e-15==" "1=rf=10.0==" "1=vbi=1.0==" "1=ld=0.1e-9==" "1=lg=0.1e-9==" "1=ls=0.1e-9==" "1=cgs=1e-12==" "1=cgd=1e-12==" "1=cds=1e-12==" "1=rin=1e-3==">
  </Symbol>
</Component>
